{
 "_comment": [
  "fairness_bands_v2 refused inputs (MISSING IS NEVER ZERO).  Both languages must REFUSE these",
  "identically -- Python raises fairness_bands.FairnessInputError, JS throws FairnessInputError, both",
  "carrying the case's code (default `code`; `expectCode` overrides) -- and never classify them",
  "(v1: JS answered 'fair' on NaN, Python 'lopsided').  Tokens, decoded the same way by both tests",
  "(JSON cannot carry NaN):",
  "  \"NaN\" / \"Infinity\" / \"-Infinity\" -> the IEEE value; \"null\" -> None / null;",
  "  \"undefined\" -> JS undefined (Python: skipped); \"str:<x>\" -> the string <x>; \"bool:true\" -> True / true;",
  "  \"object:{}\" -> an empty dict / plain object.",
  "Sections: classify(gap, base); base = fairness_base(utilities); baseContainers = fairness_base(<container>);",
  "packagePieces = the package-utility producer (Python package_utilities / larger_package_utility,",
  "JS trade-logic.js::packageUtilities + fairnessBase) on raw piece values, so a NaN piece is refused",
  "instead of being priced as an absent (0) piece.  A zero base beside |gap| >= absoluteMinimum is",
  "refused with code fairness_input_inconsistent (impossible under every package model: missing data).",
  "Accepted cases sit beside them so a refusal cannot be satisfied by refusing everything.",
  "Asserted by tests/valuation_math/test_fairness_bands.py and frontend/__tests__/fairness-bands.test.js."
 ],
